\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Balanced accuracy with which three within-event measures chose the model that was better on an independent second label, in three simulation settings. Nominal: latent risk with a fixed grid of environmental and spatial weights, runs with a spatial weight $b > 0$ only (3,720{} runs with 5~km blocks, 720{} with 20~km blocks). Tuned: spatial weight and range set per fire and environmental weight so that the null-model AUC and the matched share came close to targets taken from the real fires (279{} runs). The dashed line marks a choice no better than chance.}}{14}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:sim}{{3}{14}{Balanced accuracy with which three within-event measures chose the model that was better on an independent second label, in three simulation settings. Nominal: latent risk with a fixed grid of environmental and spatial weights, runs with a spatial weight $b > 0$ only (\sSimTenRuns {} runs with 5~km blocks, \sSimFortyRuns {} with 20~km blocks). Tuned: spatial weight and range set per fire and environmental weight so that the null-model AUC and the matched share came close to targets taken from the real fires (\sSimCalRuns {} runs). The dashed line marks a choice no better than chance}{figure.3}{}}
